# Archbee API

Archbee Sidekick integrates with the Archbee Public API.

## Source of truth

Before implementing or modifying an Archbee API integration:

- inspect the current official Archbee API documentation
- verify the endpoint
- verify authentication
- verify request format
- verify response format
- verify relevant limitations

Never infer an endpoint from an outdated example or from an LLM-generated assumption.

## Client isolation

All Archbee HTTP operations should go through the Archbee client layer.

CLI commands, analysis modules, and review UI should not make raw Archbee HTTP requests.

## Document identity

Always preserve the Archbee document ID.

Where available, also preserve:

- document title
- URL
- Space ID
- relevant metadata
- retrieved/updated timestamps

## Read operations

Reading and synchronization should be safe to repeat.

Prefer idempotent local synchronization.

The local snapshot should retain enough provenance to identify where a finding originated.

## Write operations

Writing to Archbee is a separate operation from analysis.

Never perform a write as a side effect of:

- pull
- analyze
- review
- search
- finding generation

A write must occur only after explicit user approval.

## Destructive operations

Do not implement automatic deletion.

Do not perform destructive bulk operations.

If a future feature requires deletion, require an explicit confirmation that identifies the affected documents.

## API failures

Handle:

- authentication errors
- authorization errors
- not-found responses
- validation errors
- rate limits
- network failures
- unexpected response formats

Expose actionable errors without leaking credentials.
